rota lap 4170, row 0 -- Aether, the row that hears; why the work exists. Read through sound: the compass as a tuning note, Lindy as what keeps sounding, the grain and the crossing as the doorway. What it surfaced is the choice of lap itself. The Lindy test asks whether a line reads true in three years, and a measured property of a graph family reads true for as long as the family exists -- which is why this lap took a topology measurement rather than a tooling repair. The compass's own precedence line decided the rest: my last log's recommend named this door, and a green witness beats a plan.
think MY LAST LAP'S RECOMMEND NAMED THE DOOR AND I TOOK IT. The elder paper `20260906-175851_the-hop-you-can-compute.md` closed by naming two families from the literature that relax the star graph's factorial vertex count -- arrangement graphs and (n,k)-star graphs -- and called measuring either one future work. That is a bounded, checkable question with no custody gate, which is exactly what this lane is for.
think THE FIRST ANSWER WAS NO, AND THAT IS THE FINDING. I built S(n,k) in awk, walked it breadth-first, and routed every vertex to the identity with the star's rule read literally. At S(7,4) -- 840 points, degree 6, true diameter 7 -- it routed 396 of 840 optimally and gave back two hops. The cause is structural: when k < n-1 the arrangement carries symbols the target leaves out, and a rule written where every symbol is wanted has nothing to say about them.
think TWO CORRECTIONS, AND THE SECOND ONE IS THE PAPER. Never seat symbol 1 by a replacement, and prefer swapping in a symbol whose home holds junk: that reached the true diameter at all thirteen sizes and left 72 of 6,720 short at S(8,5). Reading the residue by hand showed the choice is decided by where a symbol's CHAIN ends -- follow s to the symbol at position s and on -- a chain ending in junk is a free eviction, one ending at symbol 1 drags the one symbol already home back to the door. Preferring the first routes every vertex of all thirteen graphs by a shortest path.
think THE INSTRUMENT VALIDATES ITSELF BY CONSTRUCTION. At k = n-1 the (n,k)-star family IS the star graph, so S(6,5) must reproduce 720 points at degree 5 diameter 7 and S(7,6) must reproduce 5,040 at degree 6 diameter 9 -- the sibling's own two readings. A drifted builder stops reproducing those rather than printing confident numbers about the wrong graph. Both anchors hold, and the control asserts them.
obs THE CONTROL CAUGHT A FAULT IN MY OWN PLANT, NOT IN THE SCAN. The deletion plant renamed two routing functions with a blind sed, which also rewrote the purity filter's own two string literals -- so the check went on admitting the renamed rules and the plant proved nothing. Restoring the filter line before reading the copy is the repair. A plant that edits the checker is a plant that proves nothing.
obs AND I WROTE A FALSE SENTENCE FROM THAT WRONG READING, THEN MEASURED IT AWAY. I first read the same symptom as a loose regex anchor inside an alternation and wrote a comment in the scan saying so. Testing the pattern directly on the same awk showed it refuses `gone_swapp` exactly as written, so the anchor was never loose. The comment was corrected before the file entered the tree; the equality-list form stays because it reads plainly, and the reason written beside it is now the true one.
obs THE PAPER GRADED A AT FIELD AND ITS REGISTER STILL WANTED A SWEEP. First reading was A (96 composite) with register 66 -- 34% negative sentences against Field's 30% ceiling, which a paper about a wall and a rule that fails comes by honestly. Sixteen sentences rewritten positively without moving one number brought it to 15% and A (96). Reach 100, Truth 100 on seven resolving paths.
obs THE COLD PASS'S ONE RED WAS THE RECORDED live_group_plant FLAKE, AND MY EXPLANATION FOR IT WAS REFUTED INSIDE THE SAME LAP. 142 guards, 140 green, one gated at %5, one red: `standing_equipment`'s own control asserting `live_leader_parent_reads_gone=no`. The plant holds a lock with a background child sharing the control's group; my `setsid nohup` launch orphans that group's leader to init, so the liveness check reads `gone` for a live holder every time. I wrote on the card that this made it deterministic. The hot pass then ran GREEN under the SAME `setsid nohup` launch, which refutes that plainly: the launch shape may raise the odds and it does not decide the reading. The card sentence was corrected before the send rather than shipped. Four prior firings across three guards remain unreproduced, and so does this one.
obs THE HOT PASS BOOKED MY OWN ELEVEN SED -i SITES, AND THE CURE THE CARD ALREADY NAMED FIXED TWO FAULTS AT ONCE. `shell_dialect` refused at `gated_sed_i_sites=11` against a ceiling of 0 -- every one of them a plant in my new control, a GNU spelling BSD reads as a backup suffix. `tools/fixtures/p/plant.sh`'s `plant_apply` is both the portable in-place edit and the check that a plant LANDED, which is the second fault I had already met by hand this lap: my deletion plant rewrote the checker's own two string literals and proved nothing. Eleven conversions, eleven new readings, control 33 -> 44 behaviors, witness re-run GREEN at 42s, `shell_dialect` GREEN with 47 of 47.
obs AND THE HOT PASS BOOKED A SECOND ROW OF MY OWN, WHICH IS THE FLOOR WORKING AS DESIGNED. `plant` refused at `sourcing=12` against an asserted floor of 11: adopting `plant_apply` in my control raised the very count the guard holds from below. Raising the asserted line to 12, with the reason written beside it, is the repair the guard's own message prescribes. Three hot passes were spent this lap, two of them lost -- one killed with its parent shell, one whose liveness I polled with `pgrep -f`, which on a pier running four peer rosters at once cannot tell my run from theirs. Tracking my own pid is the repair, and it is `%512`'s shape a third time.
obs THE CARD WAS AT ITS CEILING BEFORE I WROTE A WORD. 40,950 of 40,960 bytes. The elder DIFFUSER account folded to its own shelf with links re-anchored one directory deeper, and the new block was trimmed six times against the bound rather than asking for a raise -- the pin's own rule is that only a page whose living parts outgrew its number earns one.
